{"body":"**[blocker]** PR is CONFLICTING with origin/main (mergeStateStatus DIRTY; verified twice). Main's edc0999a (#925, closes #870) refactored the very `sendStatus` block this PR moves out of rest_api.ts: it now uses the new leveled logger (`utils/logger.ts`) via a `getStatusContext` helper, while this PR deletes the block and imports `sendStatus` from `./utils/api_response`. Resolve by keeping the PR's move (drop the in-file `sendStatus`/`getStatusContext` copy per the HEAD side of the conflict) and porting main's logger-based implementation into `utils/api_response.ts` instead of the console.log variant (see the next finding), preserving the PR's added 429 switch case. The rest of the file (global fetch + Readable.fromWeb assets proxy, logger.warn calls) auto-merges cleanly.","diff_hunk":"@@ -2,21 +2,35 @@ import { Express, Request, Response } from 'express';
 import fetch from 'node-fetch';
 import Auth from './utils/auth';
 import {
-  AuthEmailRequest,
   AuthExistsResponse,
-  AuthLoginRequest,
   AuthLoginResponse,
-  AuthPasswordRequest,
-  AuthRegisterRequest,
   AuthRegistrationResponse,
   DailyGetResponse,
   DeckCard,
   DeckListResponse,
-  GenericResponse,
   ItemListResponse,
   ItemListResponseBox,
   ProfileGetResponse
 } from '../shared/interfaces/rest_api';
+import { sendStatus } from './utils/api_response';","id":4599485631,"line":null,"original_line":null,"path":"server/src/components/rest_api.ts"}
{"body":"**[minor]** Raw `console.log` with hand-built `WARN:`/`ERROR:` prefixes. AGENTS.md requires the server to log through the leveled logger utility ("never `console.*` directly"), and main now ships `server/src/components/utils/logger.ts` whose own copy of this exact function already calls `logger.warn`/`logger.error`. Replace with `logger.warn(...)` for 4xx and `logger.error(...)` for 5xx (porting main's `getStatusContext` implementation), which also removes the duplicated prefix logic here. Follow-up: the tests asserting the old behavior must be adapted — `request_validation.test.ts` spies on `console.log` (lines 204, 216, 229) and asserts `/^WARN: .*status 400/` on it (line 225), and `rest_api.test.ts` silences `console.log` in many places (e.g. lines 141, 152, 165, 195, 450, 489); the logger emits warn/error through `console.error`, so spy/silence that (as main's migrated specs do) or spy on the logger itself.","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+import { Response } from 'express';
+import { GenericResponse } from '../../shared/interfaces/rest_api';
+
+/**
+ * Sends a status response and logs error statuses with a level beforehand, so no API failure
+ * degrades silently: 4xx are logged as `WARN` (recoverable, e.g. invalid client requests) and
+ * 5xx as `ERROR` (server-side failures that need attention). Only the method and the matched
+ * route pattern are logged - never the query string or the concrete path, whose parameters
+ * may carry credentials, email addresses or one-time UUIDs.
+ * @param res response to send the status to
+ * @param status HTTP status code
+ * @param message optional response message, defaults to the status text
+ */
+export function sendStatus(res: Response, status: number, message?: string) {
+  if (status >= 400) {
+    const level = status >= 500 ? 'ERROR' : 'WARN';
+    // The matched route pattern is logged instead of the concrete path: path parameters can
+    // carry usernames, email addresses or one-time UUIDs, which must never end up in logs
+    const route = res.req?.route?.path;
+    const context = res.req ? ` for ${res.req.method}${route ? ` ${route}` : ''}` : '';
+    console.log(`${level}: API request${context} failed with status ${status}`);","id":4599485644,"line":null,"original_line":null,"path":"server/src/components/utils/api_response.ts"}
{"body":"**[nit]** Deprecated zod v4 API: the installed zod 4.6.7 marks `z.string().email()` as `@deprecated Use z.email() instead` (same for `z.string().uuid()` at line 110, deprecated in favor of `z.uuid()`). Both work today, but since this PR introduces zod brand-new, prefer the top-level formats: `z.email('Invalid email address')` with `.trim().max(60)` chained after, and `z.uuid('Invalid one-time link id')`.","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@
+import { Request, Response } from 'express';
+import { z } from 'zod';
+import { starterDecks } from '../../shared/config/starter_decks';
+import { passwordHasLetterAndDigit } from '../../shared/config/password_rules';
+import { sendStatus } from './api_response';
+
+/**
+ * Username constraints, mirrored from the registration form in the website and the
+ * `varchar(20)` column of the credentials table.
+ */
+const username = z
+  .string({ message: 'Username must be a string' })
+  .trim()
+  .min(3, 'Username must be between 3 and 20 characters long')
+  .max(20, 'Username must be between 3 and 20 characters long');
+
+/**
+ * Password strength rule for newly set passwords: 8 to 40 characters (the length also
+ * enforced by the website forms and the `varchar(40)` column) plus at least one letter and
+ * one digit. Not applied to login, where existing passwords must keep working.
+ */
+const strongPassword = z
+  .string({ message: 'Password must be a string' })
+  .min(8, 'Password must be between 8 and 40 characters long')
+  .max(40, 'Password must be between 8 and 40 characters long')
+  .refine(value => passwordHasLetterAndDigit(value), {
+    message: 'Password must contain at least one letter and one digit'
+  });
+
+/** Email constraints, mirrored from the registration form and the `varchar(60)` column. */
+const email = z
+  .string({ message: 'Email must be a string' })
+  .trim()
+  .max(60, 'Email must not be longer than 60 characters')
+  .email('Invalid email address');","id":4599485651,"line":null,"original_line":null,"path":"server/src/components/utils/request_validation.ts"}

