{"body":"**[blocker]** PR is CONFLICTING with origin/main (mergeStateStatus DIRTY; verified twice). Main's edc0999a (#925, closes #870) refactored the very `sendStatus` block this PR moves out of rest_api.ts: it now uses the new leveled logger (`utils/logger.ts`) via a `getStatusContext` helper, while this PR deletes the block and imports `sendStatus` from `./utils/api_response`. Resolve by keeping the PR's move (drop the in-file `sendStatus`/`getStatusContext` copy per the HEAD side of the conflict) and porting main's logger-based implementation into `utils/api_response.ts` instead of the console.log variant (see the next finding), preserving the PR's added 429 switch case. The rest of the file (global fetch + Readable.fromWeb assets proxy, logger.warn calls) auto-merges cleanly.","id":4599485631,"in_reply_to_id":null,"path":"server/src/components/rest_api.ts","user":"chrthom"}
{"body":"**[minor]** Raw `console.log` with hand-built `WARN:`/`ERROR:` prefixes. AGENTS.md requires the server to log through the leveled logger utility ("never `console.*` directly"), and main now ships `server/src/components/utils/logger.ts` whose own copy of this exact function already calls `logger.warn`/`logger.error`. Replace with `logger.warn(...)` for 4xx and `logger.error(...)` for 5xx (porting main's `getStatusContext` implementation), which also removes the duplicated prefix logic here. Follow-up: the tests asserting the old behavior must be adapted — `request_validation.test.ts` spies on `console.log` (lines 204, 216, 229) and asserts `/^WARN: .*status 400/` on it (line 225), and `rest_api.test.ts` silences `console.log` in many places (e.g. lines 141, 152, 165, 195, 450, 489); the logger emits warn/error through `console.error`, so spy/silence that (as main's migrated specs do) or spy on the logger itself.","id":4599485644,"in_reply_to_id":null,"path":"server/src/components/utils/api_response.ts","user":"chrthom"}
{"body":"**[nit]** Deprecated zod v4 API: the installed zod 4.6.7 marks `z.string().email()` as `@deprecated Use z.email() instead` (same for `z.string().uuid()` at line 110, deprecated in favor of `z.uuid()`). Both work today, but since this PR introduces zod brand-new, prefer the top-level formats: `z.email('Invalid email address')` with `.trim().max(60)` chained after, and `z.uuid('Invalid one-time link id')`.","id":4599485651,"in_reply_to_id":null,"path":"server/src/components/utils/request_validation.ts","user":"chrthom"}

